# TRANSLATION ONLY. This file exists for one case: translating without spending
# the Claude subscription window. It can configure nothing else — the loader in
# teach/core/__init__.py accepts the five variables below and refuses the rest,
# out loud.
#
# In particular it CANNOT change the authoring backend. `TEACH_BACKEND=...` here
# does nothing, on purpose: authoring decides what is true and is worth the
# strongest model available, and moving it to a cheap model would be invisible
# afterwards except in the meta.yaml of every topic written while it was set.
# To change what authors, pass `--backend` or set TEACH_BACKEND in the real
# environment, where it is a visible decision.
#
#     cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env && $EDITOR .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored, loaded automatically by teach/core/__init__.py, and read
# by every entry point — CLI, scripts and the timer alike. Variables already set
# in the environment always win, so this file is a default and never an override.
#
# WITHOUT this file everything still works: translation falls back to `claude`.
# That is the current, deliberate setup. This exists for the day the trade stops
# being worth it — see the numbers below.
#
# Two things to know, since the key lives in the working tree:
#   - This repository sits inside a Nextcloud folder, so `.env` syncs to the
#     Nextcloud server and every device attached to it. git-ignoring it does not
#     change that. Treat the key as present on all of them.
#   - The pre-commit hook refuses to commit a populated `.env` or a key pasted
#     into any other file. It is a backstop, not the protection: `--no-verify`
#     and a fresh clone both bypass it. The repository is public, so a key that
#     is ever pushed must be rotated, not deleted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- why

# Authoring and translation are not the same job. Authoring decides what is true
# and is worth the strongest model available; translation has its substance fixed
# by the source, and every way it can fail is mechanically detectable
# (`_verify_translation` checks code blocks, URLs, headings and length).
#
# Measured in docs/TRANSLATION_STUDY.md: the whole remaining translation workload
# costs about $0.07 on OpenRouter. The saving is NOT money — on a subscription
# the dollar figures are an API-equivalent price, not a bill. The saving is the
# ~5 h quota window, which is the actual finite resource: every window spent
# translating is a window not spent authoring, and authoring cannot be made
# cheaper without making it worse.
#
# If the trade ever stops being worth it, fall back to `--backend claude` for
# translation too — never the reverse. Authoring on a cheap model is the one
# substitution this project does not make.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what to set

# Where the OpenAI-compatible API lives.
#
#   OpenRouter direct:  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   Cluster LiteLLM:    https://litellm.cluster.home/v1
#
# Note on the cluster proxy: litellm.cluster.home resolves to the gateway VIP
# 192.168.178.200, and that VIP did not answer from the Toolbx container on
# 2026-08-13 even though kubectl worked (kubectl talks to the API server on
# .120, not to the gateway). If it still does not answer, port-forward instead
# and point the URL at localhost:
#
#     kubectl port-forward -n ai svc/litellm-proxy 14000:4000
#     LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:14000/v1
LITELLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# OpenRouter key, or LITELLM_MASTER_KEY from the cluster proxy pod.
LITELLM_API_KEY=

# The model. Translation is the one place a cheap model is measured safe.
# `gpt-5.4-mini` ran out of credit after two topics with a 402 on 2026-08-06
# (Antigravity's note in AGENTS_SYNC.md), so check credit before assuming a
# paid route works; a free route avoids the question entirely.
LITELLM_MODEL=gemini-free

# Send translation — and ONLY translation — to the above. Authoring keeps using
# whatever `--backend` says, which is `claude` by default.
TEACH_TRANSLATE_BACKEND=litellm

# CLI-agent backends can be slow on long documents; the default timeout is short
# enough to cut a translation off mid-way. Antigravity hit this before the model
# was even at fault.
OPENAI_TIMEOUT=600
